    "https://www.vacancies.aau.dk/scientific-positions/show-vacancy/vacancyId/982334": {
      "title": "Postdoc in Learning-Based Multi-Agent Control under Uncertainty",
      "description": "Postdoc in Learning-Based Multi-Agent Control under Uncertainty - Aalborg University Jump to content Vacant positions at Aalborg University Scientific positions Application requirements Recruitment process Career options PhD positions Application requirements PhD Schools Career options Recruitment process Technical or administrative positions Application requirements Appointment and assessment Career options AAU as a workplace Change language DA Search Vacant positions Scientific positions Show vacancy Postdoc in Learning-Based Multi-Agent Control under Uncertainty Apply Vacant position Postdoc in Learning-Based Multi-Agent Control under Uncertainty Aalborg Deadline : 05.11.2026 Department: Department of Electronic Systems Ref number: 2026/1221 Employment type: Full Time Apply Aalborg Deadline : 05.11.2026 Department: Department of Electronic Systems Ref number: 2026/1221 Employment type: Full Time Apply Vacant position Postdoc in Learning-Based Multi-Agent Control under Uncertainty Aalborg Deadline : 05.11.2026 Department: Department of Electronic Systems Ref number: 2026/1221 Employment type: Full Time Apply Aalborg Deadline : 05.11.2026 Department: Department of Electronic Systems Ref number: 2026/1221 Employment type: Full Time Apply The Department of Electronic Systems at the Technical Faculty of IT and Design invites applications for a postdoc in learning-based multi-agent control under uncertainty, with applications to autonomous multi-robot systems operating in dynamic and uncertain environments, as per February 1, 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. The position is available for a period of 2 years. Your work tasks The position focuses on fundamental research in learning-based planning and control of interacting autonomous agents under uncertainty. You will develop new theoretical and algorithmic approaches for distributed and cooperative control, combining learning or online adaptation with principled treatment of safety, robustness, and performance. Research challenges include uncertain dynamics and disturbances, partial or noisy information, changing interactions between agents, and limited or unreliable communication. A central part of the work will be to formulate rigorous methods and establish their properties, for example concerning stability, safety, constraint satisfaction, robustness, and convergence, where applicable. Depending on the research direction, the work may draw on learning-augmented model predictive control, safe reinforcement learning, data-driven modelling and safety mechanism (e.g. CBF), distributed optimization, or robust and adaptive control. You will develop reproducible numerical studies and simulations to examine the strengths, limitations, and scalability of the proposed methods. The research will be carried out in the Horizon Europe ROX-6G project, where heterogeneous robot teams provide a compelling application for coordination under uncertain conditions and connectivity constraints. Although the position is primarily theoretical, you will collaborate with colleagues working on robotic implementation and will contribute to experimental validation. You will lead and co-author publications in international journals and conferences, engage with project partners, contribute to research planning and scientific discussions, and support knowledge exchange within the team. Your competencies We seek a researcher with a PhD in control engineering, robotics, electrical engineering, applied mathematics, computer science, or a closely related field, and a strong background in mathematical modelling, control, optimization, or multi-agent systems. You should be able to formulate original research problems, develop and analyse rigorous methods, and demonstrate research quality through peer-reviewed scientific publications. Experience in learning-based control, robust or nonlinear control, distributed control, or decision-making under uncertainty is particularly relevant; expertise in every one of these areas is not expected. You should have good scientific programming skills, for example in Python, MATLAB, or C++, and be able to evaluate algorithms systematically through simulation. We value independent research initiative, clear scientific writing, and the ability to work constructively with researchers from different disciplines and backgrounds. Experience with autonomous robots, ROS/ROS 2, multi-robot simulation, or physical robotic experiments will be considered an advantage, but is not a prerequisite for this primarily theory-oriented position. Excellent written and spoken English is required. Who we are In electronic engineering, Aalborg University is known worldwide for its high academic quality and societal impact. The Department of Electronic Systems employs more than 200 people, of which about 90 are PhD students, and about 40 % of all employees are internationals. In total, it has more than 600 students in its BSc and MSc programs, which are based on AAU's problem-based learning model. The department leverages its unique research infrastructure and lab facilities to conduct world-leading fundamental and applied research within communication, networks, control systems, AI, sound, cyber security, and robotics. The department plays an active role in transferring inventions and results into applications in close collaboration with industrial partners worldwide. You can read more about the department at www.es.aau.dk. The position is hosted in the Automation and Control Section, within a collaborative robotics research environment combining fundamental research with real-world applications. In addition, you will work with an international team and research partners in ROX-6G, a European collaboration addressing autonomous robotic operations in demanding underground environments. Our research interests span safe and resilient decision-making, learning-enabled control, distributed multi-robot coordination, and validation in simulation and on robotic platforms. We encourage scientific independence, close exchange of ideas, and publication of high-quality research. More information: www.es.aau.dk. Qualification requirements Appointment as postdoc requires academic qualifications at PhD level. How to apply Your application must include the following: Application, stating reasons for applying, qualifications in relation to the position, and intentions and visions for the position Curriculum Vitae (CV) Diplomas (master's degree diploma and PhD diploma) List of publications, with an indication of the attached publications that you wish to be taken into account in the assessment. You may attach a maximum of five publications. Documentation of teaching qualifications if relevant. Dissemination qualifications, including participation on committees or boards, participation in organisations etc. Additional qualifications in relation to the position References/recommendations You can read more about the requirements for your application here . The application must be submitted via Aalborg University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aalborg University's website. Aalborg University wants to reflect the surrounding society and has diversity as a core value. Therefore, everyone, regardless of personal background and orientation, is encouraged to apply for the position. Aalborg University has a policy of parallel language use. International staff are encouraged, with support from the university, to learn Danish during their employment in order to support their integration into the workplace and Danish society. Danish language courses will be offered as part of the employment. Do you have any questions? If you have any questions about the position, you are more than welcome to contact us. You will find contact persons at the bottom of the jobpost. Further information Read more about our recruitment process here The appointment process at Aalborg University involves a shortlisting process. You can read more about the shortlisting and appointment process here . The hiring process at Aalborg University may include a risk assessment as a tool to identify potential risks associated with new hires, ensuring the safety, compliance, and integrity of the workplace. Salary and terms of employment The employment is in accordance with the Ministerial Order on the Appointment of Academic Staff at Universities and the Ministerial Order on Job Structure for Academic Staff at Universities. Furthermore, your terms of employment and salary are in accordance with the collective agreement between the Danish Confederation of Professional Associations and the state (AC collective agreement) and protocol on certain terms of employment of academic staff at universities. You can find information about the salary and salary structure for the position in the Salary Overview for Recruitment - Scientific positions (VIP) . Please refer to the introductory section of the page and the section entitled “Postdoc”. Aalborg University - Knowledge for the world Aalborg University is an international workplace with more than 3,700 employees. We offer real-world-oriented education and create world-class research results through collaboration between researchers, students, and public and private companies. This is how we achieve insights, new solutions to societal problems, and knowledge that changes the world. Our main campus is in Aalborg, but we also have campuses in Esbjerg and Copenhagen. Contacts Shahab Heshmati-Alamdari: +4599403451, shhe@es.aau.dk HR Support : Aau-hrsupport@adm.aau.dk Employment type Full time Ref number 2026/1221 Deadline 05.11.2026 Apply Employment and assessment Contact Contact Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 About AAU About AAU About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact Shortcuts Shortcuts EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions Service About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme"
    },
    "https://www.vacancies.aau.dk/scientific-positions/show-vacancy/vacancyId/982910": {
      "title": "Tenure track Assistant Professor in Medical Protein Science",
      "description": "Tenure track Assistant Professor in Medical Protein Science - Aalborg University Jump to content Vacant positions at Aalborg University Scientific positions Application requirements Recruitment process Career options PhD positions Application requirements PhD Schools Career options Recruitment process Technical or administrative positions Application requirements Appointment and assessment Career options AAU as a workplace Change language DA Search Vacant positions Scientific positions Show vacancy Tenure track Assistant Professor in Medical Protein Science Apply Vacant position Tenure track Assistant Professor in Medical Protein Science Aalborg Deadline : 06.11.2026 Department: Department of Chemistry and Bioscience Ref number: 2026/1228 Employment type: Full Time Apply Aalborg Deadline : 06.11.2026 Department: Department of Chemistry and Bioscience Ref number: 2026/1228 Employment type: Full Time Apply Vacant position Tenure track Assistant Professor in Medical Protein Science Aalborg Deadline : 06.11.2026 Department: Department of Chemistry and Bioscience Ref number: 2026/1228 Employment type: Full Time Apply Aalborg Deadline : 06.11.2026 Department: Department of Chemistry and Bioscience Ref number: 2026/1228 Employment type: Full Time Apply Do you want to work with medical protein science? And do you see yourself as a team player who is strong in collaboration? If yes, we look forward to reading your application to our position as Tenure track Assistant Professor. At the Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, a position as Tenure Track Assistant Professor within the field of Medical Biotechnology with focus on medical protein science is open for appointment from 1 February 2027 or soon hereafter. Tenure track assistant professors are appointed for a period of six years with the prospect of performance-based promotion to a tenured position as Associate Professor. The position is affiliated with the Section of Medical Biotechnology, with workplace in Aalborg, Denmark. Medical biotechnology is a highly interdisciplinary field that applies and develops biotechnological tools to improve the diagnosis and treatment of diseases and to advance our understanding of their underlying molecular mechanisms. Your work tasks Within the Section of Medical Biotechnology, our current research focuses on the molecular mechanisms underlying ageing and age-related diseases, cardiovascular and neurological diseases, cancer and circulating tumour cells, obesity-related complications, and calcium signaling. We employ both in vitro and in vivo approaches, including cell and animal models, directed evolution of proteins, protein engineering, and biophysical characterization. We are seeking an outstanding candidate who will strengthen and complement our research environment within the area of medical protein science. Particular emphasis will be placed on documented experience in protein expression, production, purification, and characterization using both in vitro and in vivo approaches. Relevant prioritized expertise includes but is not limited to: i) Protein purification using chromatographic techniques, including affinity, hydrophobic interaction, ion-exchange, and size-exclusion chromatography. ii) Functional characterization of proteins and protein-ligand interactions using techniques such as absorbance and fluorescence spectroscopy, fluorescence anisotropy, isothermal titration calorimetry, biolayer interferometry, and microscale thermophoresis. Regarding research activities, you will be expected to establish and lead an independent research group, secure external research funding, and publish your findings in internationally recognized peer-reviewed journals. A key responsibility will be to strengthen and further develop the Department's laboratory facilities and research infrastructure in protein science, supporting both research excellence and educational activities. You are also expected to develop national and international research collaborations, contribute to interdisciplinary research initiatives, and participate in relevant academic networks. As a member of the teaching team at the Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, you will contribute to teaching and course development, as well as supervise undergraduate and graduate students and student groups. You are furthermore expected to contribute to the continuous development of study programmes and teaching activities. In addition, you will be expected to contribute to departmental activities such as strategic communication, student recruitment, outreach, and other tasks that support the department’s development and visibility. This may include participation in committees and working groups, support for quality assurance and accreditation activities, mentorship of junior colleagues, organization of scientific events, and engagement with external stakeholders, including industry and public-sector partners. The Department of Chemistry and Bioscience offers highly qualified candidates an attractive career path through its tenure-track program. Tenure-track assistant professors are appointed with the possibility of promotion to a tenured Associate Professorship based on a positive evaluation of academic performance and academic citizenship. Assistant professors employed on tenure-track will participate in annual development and evaluation meetings with the Head of Department. A positive final evaluation will result in an offer of permanent employment as Associate Professor. The assessment will be based on the candidate's progress relative to the agreed tenure-track plan and an overall evaluation of achievements within research, teaching, external funding, collaboration, academic citizenship and leadership. Your Competenties Applicants should have a relevant academic background within the research area. Have a strong interest in working in an interdisciplinary research environment. Conduct high-quality experimental research in medical biotechnology, both independently and in close collaboration with existing research groups within the department. Demonstrate international research potential and develop an independent academic profile that complements and strengthens the department’s existing research areas. Establish and develop collaborations with relevant research environments across Aalborg University and Aalborg University Hospital. Actively pursue competitive external research funding and contribute to the department’s overall research strategy and development. Contribute to high-quality scientific publications and dissemination of research results. Contribute to research-based teaching and supervision of student projects, including student-centered and project-based learning (PBL), which is an integral part of Aalborg University’s educational model Qualification requirements Applicants for a tenure track assistant professorship must have academic qualifications at PhD level. When appointing tenure track assistant professors, Aalborg University also place particular emphasis on: The candidate can demonstrate a high degree of autonomy in their previous education and employment path The candidate shows considerable potential and is among the best in their field The candidate has academic experience from several universities and/or research institutions and preferably international experience The candidate is a skilled communicator The candidate writes and speaks English at the academic level The candidate is expected to meet the criteria for permanent employment as an associate professor at Aalborg University at the end of the tenure track process Innovation and academic citizenship Applicants are encouraged to document relevant qualifications and achievements within innovation and academic citizenship. This may include experience with innovation, knowledge transfer and collaboration with external partners, as well as contributions to the academic community through collegial collaboration, committees, boards, working groups, mentoring and organizational development. Relevant qualifications and achievements within these areas will be considered as part of the overall assessment of the applicant in relation to the requirements of the position. Who we are At the Department of Chemistry and Bioscience (BIO), our high-level research spans from basic to applied within both natural sciences and engineering. With approx. 200 employees, 75 PhD students, and 775 bachelor and master’s students at our campuses in Aalborg (main campus) and Esbjerg, we are a vital research and educational institution when it comes to creating new basic knowledge as well as contributing to solving the world’s challenges within biology, chemistry, biotechnology, bioengineering, environmental science, and chemical engineering. We continuously improve our department as an attractive place of work and study. We offer flexible hours, social activities throughout the year both at the department level and in each Section. We are inclusive and have respect for individuals, communities, and cultures. Our work culture is founded on openness, curiosity, transparency, and involvement. Come join us! Read more about the department here; Welcome to the Department of Chemistry and Bioscience - en.bio.aau.dk - Aalborg University Assessment in connection with transfer to associate professorship The assessment in connection with transition to tenure as an associate professor normally takes place in the final six months of the tenure track assistant professors’ employment. However, the employee may request that an assessment take place at an earlier time in the first four years. If this assessment finds that the employee is not academically qualified, they may request another assessment within the final six months of their period of employment. A maximum of two assessments may take place. The assessment, on transition to the associate professorship, will as a minimum, emphasize the following qualifications in relation to the scientific subject area of the tenure track assistant professorship: Research qualifications equivalent to the level that can be achieved on the basis of satisfactorily completed employment as tenure track assistant professor. Documented scientific production at international level. Assessment will be based on up to ten selected publications selected by the employee. Documentation of pedagogical supervision and upgrading of qualifications, including a positive written assessment of teaching qualifications. The assessment will also be based on the employee's teaching portfolio. The level of contribution to an active academic environment as well as the ability to collaborate and build relationships. The level of experience with grant proposals and experience of communicating research to relevant stakeholders. If the tenure track assistant professor fails to request that their qualifications be assessed in the last year of their period of employment or if they are assessed as not academically qualified, the university must immediately initiate dismissal proceedings in accordance with the collective agreement rules. How to apply Your application must include the following: Application, stating reasons for applying, qualifications in relation to the position, and intentions and visions for the position Curriculum Vitae (CV) Diplomas (master's degree diploma and PhD diploma) List of publications, with an indication of the attached publications that you wish to be taken into account in the assessment. You may attach a maximum of five publications. Documentation of teaching qualifications. Please see guidelines for teaching portfolio at The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, The Faculty of Engineering and Science and The Faculty of Medicine. If this is not enclosed, the applicant must enclose the reasons for this . Dissemination qualifications, including participation on committees or boards, participation in organisations etc. Additional qualifications in relation to the position References/recommendations You can read more about the requirements for your application here . The application must be submitted via Aalborg University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aalborg University's website. Aalborg University wants to reflect the surrounding society and has diversity as a core value. Therefore, everyone, regardless of personal background and orientation, is encouraged to apply for the position. Aalborg University has a policy of parallel language use. The successful applicant is expected, with support from the university, to acquire Danish language skills over time and to be able to contribute to teaching in Danish within 2–5 years of employment, including grading and supervising students, at a level corresponding to the teaching undertaken. Danish language courses will be offered as part of the employment. Do you have any questions? If you have any questions about the position, you are more than welcome to contact us. You will find contact persons at the bottom of the jobpost. Further information Read more about our recruitment process here The appointment process at Aalborg University involves a shortlisting process. You can read more about the shortlisting and appointment process here . The hiring process at Aalborg University may include a risk assessment as a tool to identify potential risks associated with new hires, ensuring the safety, compliance, and integrity of the workplace. Salary and terms of employment The employment is in accordance with the Ministerial Order on the Appointment of Academic Staff at Universities and the Ministerial Order on Job Structure for Academic Staff at Universities. Furthermore, your terms of employment and salary are in accordance with the collective agreement between the Danish Confederation of Professional Associations and the state (AC collective agreement) and protocol on certain terms of employment of academic staff at universities. You can find information about the salary and salary structure for the position in the Salary Overview for Recruitment - Scientific positions (VIP) . Please refer to the introductory section of the page and the section entitled “Tenure track assistant professor/Tenure track researcher”. There is a mutual probationary period of 3 months for the position. Aalborg University - Knowledge for the world Aalborg University is an international workplace with more than 3,700 employees. We offer real-world-oriented education and create world-class research results through collaboration between researchers, students, and public and private companies. This is how we achieve insights, new solutions to societal problems, and knowledge that changes the world. Our main campus is in Aalborg, but we also have campuses in Esbjerg and Copenhagen. Contacts Associate Professor Anders Olsen: +4599408043, ao@bio.aau.dk HR Support: aau-hrsupport@adm.aau.dk Employment type Full time Ref number 2026/1228 Deadline 06.11.2026 Apply Employment and assessment Contact Contact Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 About AAU About AAU About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact Shortcuts Shortcuts EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions Service About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme"
    },
    "https://www.vacancies.aau.dk/scientific-positions/show-vacancy/vacancyId/982420": {
      "title": "Postdoc in Energy System Analysis",
      "description": "Postdoc in Energy System Analysis - Aalborg University Jump to content Vacant positions at Aalborg University Scientific positions Application requirements Recruitment process Career options PhD positions Application requirements PhD Schools Career options Recruitment process Technical or administrative positions Application requirements Appointment and assessment Career options AAU as a workplace Change language DA Search Vacant positions Scientific positions Show vacancy Postdoc in Energy System Analysis Apply Vacant position Postdoc in Energy System Analysis Copenhagen Deadline : 09.11.2026 Department: Department of Sustainability and Planning Ref number: 2026/1223 Employment type: Full Time Apply Copenhagen Deadline : 09.11.2026 Department: Department of Sustainability and Planning Ref number: 2026/1223 Employment type: Full Time Apply Vacant position Postdoc in Energy System Analysis Copenhagen Deadline : 09.11.2026 Department: Department of Sustainability and Planning Ref number: 2026/1223 Employment type: Full Time Apply Copenhagen Deadline : 09.11.2026 Department: Department of Sustainability and Planning Ref number: 2026/1223 Employment type: Full Time Apply At the Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Sustainability and Planning, Copenhagen, a position as Postdoc in Energy System Analysis is open for appointment from 1 February 2027 or soon hereafter. The position is a 2-year Post Doc. The department was established in 1975. Today, we are located in two beautiful harbour-front locations in both Aalborg and Copenhagen. We have more than 250 employees and approximately 1,200 students across the two cities. Our research and study programmes are rooted in sustainability and the green transition. This means we conduct research in areas such as the circular economy, technology, urban, energy, and environmental planning, as well as sustainable transition and design. Sustainability is central to our work in environmental assessment and marine management. In surveying and land use, sustainability is reflected in our efforts in nature restoration and climate adaptation. As society continues to develop digitally, we also focus on responsible technology development, addressing real-life challenges. Our problem-oriented approach and close collaboration with businesses and public organisations form the foundation of all our study programmes. Additionally, our engineering programmes are among the best in Europe. Job description The Postdoctoral Researcher position focuses on energy system analysis and tool development, with particular emphasis on energy system modelling across multiple scales (European, national, regional) and the application of energy systems analysis within a problem-based learning (PBL) environment. The candidate will contribute to a number of research and educational projects, strengthening the integration of research activities with the development of teaching materials and learning activities for bachelor-level courses. Therefore, it is expected that the candidate can teach in Danish. The use of the energy systems simulation models EnergyPLAN and EnergyPRO is a cornerstone in the work, thus experience with this tool and model linking with other tools is a pivotal strength for applications to this position. Applicants with a relevant background or experience with other system analysis tools are also encouraged to apply for this position. The position includes teaching and supervision responsibilities within the field of energy systems and sustainability, primarily in the bachelor programmes offered by the Department of Sustainability and Planning. Applicants are expected to have documented experience in teaching and student supervision at university level. You may obtain further professional information from Professor Brian Vad Mathiesen, +45 9940 7218, bvm@plan.aau.dk You can read more on TECH as a workplace here You can read more on Department of Sustainability and Planning here Qualification requirements Appointment as Postdoc presupposes scientific qualifications at PhD–level or similar scientific qualifications. The research potential of each applicant will be emphasized in the overall assessment. Appointment as a Postdoc cannot exceed a period of four years in total at Aalborg University How to apply Your application must include the following: Application, stating reasons for applying, qualifications in relation to the position, and intentions and visions for the position Curriculum Vitae (CV) Diplomas (master's degree diploma and PhD diploma) List of publications, with an indication of the attached publications that you wish to be taken into account in the assessment. You may attach a maximum of five publications. Documentation of teaching qualifications if relevant. Dissemination qualifications, including participation on committees or boards, participation in organisations etc. Additional qualifications in relation to the position References/recommendations You can read more about the requirements for your application here . The application must be submitted via Aalborg University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aalborg University's website. Aalborg University wants to reflect the surrounding society and has diversity as a core value. Therefore, everyone, regardless of personal background and orientation, is encouraged to apply for the position. Aalborg University has a policy of parallel language use. International staff are encouraged, with support from the university, to learn Danish during their employment in order to support their integration into the workplace and Danish society. Danish language courses will be offered as part of the employment. Do you have any questions? If you have any questions about the position, you are more than welcome to contact us. You will find contact persons at the bottom of the jobpost. Further information Read more about our recruitment process here The appointment process at Aalborg University involves a shortlisting process. You can read more about the shortlisting and appointment process here . The hiring process at Aalborg University may include a risk assessment as a tool to identify potential risks associated with new hires, ensuring the safety, compliance, and integrity of the workplace. Salary and terms of employment The employment is in accordance with the Ministerial Order on the Appointment of Academic Staff at Universities and the Ministerial Order on Job Structure for Academic Staff at Universities. Furthermore, your terms of employment and salary are in accordance with the collective agreement between the Danish Confederation of Professional Associations and the state (AC collective agreement) and protocol on certain terms of employment of academic staff at universities. You can find information about the salary and salary structure for the position in the Salary Overview for Recruitment - Scientific positions (VIP) . Please refer to the introductory section of the page and the section entitled “Postdoc”. There is a mutual probationary period of 3 months for the position. Aalborg University Aalborg University (AAU) provides outstanding research and education. We believe that knowledge can and should change the world. This belief drives our high ambitions. We seek knowledge through interaction with the world around us, focusing on real problems and missions that we aim to solve with sustainable solutions. Our research and study programmes are multidisciplinary and built on close collaborations with business and industry. This approach is further strengthened by our renowned teaching model, Problem-Based Learning (PBL), which is centred on real-world problems in all their complexity. Through interdisciplinarity, industry collaboration, and world-class research, we contribute new insights, solutions to societal challenges, and knowledge that transforms the world. In 2024, AAU advanced from a position in the global Top 10 to a place in the global Top 5 for sustainability. Additionally, in the internationally recognised Times Higher Education Impact Rankings, AAU is ranked fourth among nearly 1,600 universities worldwide. This ranking assesses universities’ contributions to achieving the UN’s Sustainable Development Goals. More than 18,000 students are enrolled at Aalborg University, with over 7% being international students. To support them, we have 3,500 staff members, divided between Aalborg University’s main campus in Aalborg and our campuses in Copenhagen and Esbjerg. Aalborg University - Knowledge for the world Aalborg University is an international workplace with more than 3,700 employees. We offer real-world-oriented education and create world-class research results through collaboration between researchers, students, and public and private companies. This is how we achieve insights, new solutions to societal problems, and knowledge that changes the world. Our main campus is in Aalborg, but we also have campuses in Esbjerg and Copenhagen. Contacts Brian Vad Mathiesen: 99407218, bvm@plan.aau.dk HR Support: 99403031, HR-support@adm.aau.dk Employment type Full time Ref number 2026/1223 Deadline 09.11.2026 Apply Employment and assessment Contact Contact Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 About AAU About AAU About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact Shortcuts Shortcuts EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions Service About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme"
    },
