    "https://www.vacancies.aau.dk/scientific-positions/show-vacancy/vacancyId/981424": {
      "title": "Postdoc",
      "description": "Postdoc – Lighting Design - Aalborg University Jump to content Vacant positions at Aalborg University Scientific positions Application requirements Recruitment process Career options PhD positions Application requirements PhD Schools Career options Recruitment process Technical or administrative positions Application requirements Appointment and assessment Career options AAU as a workplace Change language DA Search Vacant positions Scientific positions Show vacancy Postdoc – Lighting Design Apply Vacant position Postdoc – Lighting Design Copenhagen Deadline : 10.11.2026 Department: Department of Architecture Ref number: 2026/1214 Employment type: Full Time Apply Copenhagen Deadline : 10.11.2026 Department: Department of Architecture Ref number: 2026/1214 Employment type: Full Time Apply Vacant position Postdoc – Lighting Design Copenhagen Deadline : 10.11.2026 Department: Department of Architecture Ref number: 2026/1214 Employment type: Full Time Apply Copenhagen Deadline : 10.11.2026 Department: Department of Architecture Ref number: 2026/1214 Employment type: Full Time Apply At Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology (Copenhagen Campus) a full-time position as Postdoc is available for a period of 2 years from February 1, 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. The Department of Architecture, Design, and Media Technology has as its goal the development of an innovative cluster of engineering-based environments for education and research which integrate creativity, engineering and technology within the disciplines of architecture, urban design, industrial design, lighting design, digital design and interactive media. The department is a leading research and educational environment in Denmark that addresses the challenge of the interplay between creativity and technology and develops new areas in research and education directed towards the end-user. Your work tasks The successful candidate will contribute to research, supervision, teaching, and semester coordination within Lighting Design at the Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Aalborg University, Copenhagen. Research activities will be conducted with the transdisciplinary Lighting Design Lab and will primarily contribute to externally funded research projects addressing societal challenges through lighting design, technology, and human-centric approaches. Supervision responsibilities will primarily be associated with the MSc program in Lighting Design, which includes approximately 60 international students. Students work in project groups on semester-based lighting design projects and individually or in groups on master theses. The projects are grounded in a strong understanding of design-research processes and integrate theories, methods, and approaches across relevant academic disciplines. The position will also include coordination of semesters and related educational activities. Teaching will primarily focus on the engineering and technical aspects of lighting design, particularly within courses such as Lighting Fundamentals and Evidence-Based Lighting Design. Topics include fundamental photometric and colorimetric concepts, lighting laws and principles, measurement quantities and methods, international standards, and objective methods for the measurement, observation, analysis, and evaluation of lighting conditions. Your competencies The successful candidate is expected to demonstrate the ability to identify emerging societal challenges and translate them into future competence and skill requirements for the lighting design profession. The candidate should also demonstrate an understanding of how these competences and skills can be integrated into teaching and research in lighting design at the highest academic level. The candidate should demonstrate the ability to attract external research funding and to lead or contribute to interdisciplinary research projects involving multiple partners and stakeholders. Experience with innovation and cross-sector collaboration between academia, industry, and public-sector organizations is considered particularly relevant. The candidate must have experience in relevant teaching and supervising diverse student groups, with a focus on developing an understanding of transdisciplinary design processes supported by relevant technical skills and a strong scientific foundation . The candidate must demonstrate strong collaborative skills and the ability to work effectively as part of an international and interdisciplinary team of lighting designers, architects, engineers, and other researchers within the Lighting Design Lab in Copenhagen. Who we are The Lighting Design Lab brings together lighting designers, engineers, architects, and researchers who work collaboratively to advance teaching and research in lighting design. The Lab supports a two-year international MSc programme in Lighting Design and a strong transdisciplinary research environment. Our work integrates architecture, engineering, AI, and media technology and is often conducted in collaboration with private-sector partners to address relevant societal challenges. Research and experimental activities combine contextual and architectural analysis of the light environment, including daylight and electric lighting, with consideration of human visual and non-visual needs and dynamic lighting conditions. Design solutions are based on a perceived understanding of light environments supported by advanced technologies such as lighting control, sensing systems, sky scanners, and smartphone-based applications, while remaining grounded in human and societal needs. The Lab also maintains a strong international network and collaborates with leading universities and research environments within lighting design. You may read more about the department here: https://www.create.aau.dk/om-create Qualification requirements Appointment as postdoc requires academic qualifications at PhD level. How to apply Your application must include the following: Application, stating reasons for applying, qualifications in relation to the position, and intentions and visions for the position Curriculum Vitae (CV) Diplomas (master's degree diploma and PhD diploma) List of publications, with an indication of the attached publications that you wish to be taken into account in the assessment. You may attach a maximum of five publications. Documentation of teaching qualifications if relevant. Dissemination qualifications, including participation on committees or boards, participation in organisations etc. Additional qualifications in relation to the position References/recommendations You can read more about the requirements for your application here . The application must be submitted via Aalborg University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aalborg University's website. Aalborg University wants to reflect the surrounding society and has diversity as a core value. Therefore, everyone, regardless of personal background and orientation, is encouraged to apply for the position. Aalborg University has a policy of parallel language use. International staff are encouraged, with support from the university, to learn Danish during their employment in order to support their integration into the workplace and Danish society. Danish language courses will be offered as part of the employment. Do you have any questions? If you have any questions about the position, you are more than welcome to contact associate professor Ellen Kathrine Hansen, ekh@create.aau.dk Phone: 0045 21723181 Further information Read more about our recruitment process here The appointment process at Aalborg University involves a shortlisting process. You can read more about the shortlisting and appointment process here . The hiring process at Aalborg University may include a risk assessment as a tool to identify potential risks associated with new hires, ensuring the safety, compliance, and integrity of the workplace. Salary and terms of employment The employment is in accordance with the Ministerial Order on the Appointment of Academic Staff at Universities and the Ministerial Order on Job Structure for Academic Staff at Universities. Furthermore, your terms of employment and salary are in accordance with the collective agreement between the Danish Confederation of Professional Associations and the state (AC collective agreement) and protocol on certain terms of employment of academic staff at universities. You can find information about the salary and salary structure for the position in the Salary Overview for Recruitment - Scientific positions (VIP) . Please refer to the introductory section of the page and the section entitled “Postdoc”. There is a mutual probationary period of 3 months for the position. Aalborg University - Knowledge for the world Aalborg University is an international workplace with more than 3,700 employees. We offer real-world-oriented education and create world-class research results through collaboration between researchers, students, and public and private companies. This is how we achieve insights, new solutions to societal problems, and knowledge that changes the world. Our main campus is in Aalborg, but we also have campuses in Esbjerg and Copenhagen. Employment type Full time Ref number 2026/1214 Deadline 10.11.2026 Apply Employment and assessment Contact Contact Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 About AAU About AAU About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact Shortcuts Shortcuts EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions Service About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme"
    },
    "https://www.vacancies.aau.dk/scientific-positions/show-vacancy/vacancyId/982518": {
      "title": "Postdoc i Implemeneringsvidenskab indenfor lungemedicin",
      "description": "Postdoc i Implemeneringsvidenskab indenfor lungemedicin - Aalborg University Jump to content Vacant positions at Aalborg University Scientific positions Application requirements Recruitment process Career options PhD positions Application requirements PhD Schools Career options Recruitment process Technical or administrative positions Application requirements Appointment and assessment Career options AAU as a workplace Change language DA Search Vacant positions Scientific positions Show vacancy Postdoc i Implemeneringsvidenskab indenfor lungemedicin Apply Vacant position Postdoc i Implemeneringsvidenskab indenfor lungemedicin Aalborg Deadline : 15.11.2026 Department: Klinisk Institut Ref number: 2026/1227 Employment type: Full Time Apply Aalborg Deadline : 15.11.2026 Department: Klinisk Institut Ref number: 2026/1227 Employment type: Full Time Apply Vacant position Postdoc i Implemeneringsvidenskab indenfor lungemedicin Aalborg Deadline : 15.11.2026 Department: Klinisk Institut Ref number: 2026/1227 Employment type: Full Time Apply Aalborg Deadline : 15.11.2026 Department: Klinisk Institut Ref number: 2026/1227 Employment type: Full Time Apply Ved Klinisk Institut på Aalborg Universitet er en treårig fuldtidsstilling som postdoc ledig til besættelse pr. 1. januar 2027 eller snarest derefter. Som postdoc bliver du en del af et voksende og dynamisk forskningsmiljø ved det nyetablerede Center for Implementeringsvidenskab og Lungemedicinsk Forskningsenhed på Aalborg Universitetshospital. Her får du mulighed for at bidrage til forskning med fokus på lokalsamfundsinddragelse og implementeringsvidenskab inden for kroniske lungesygdomme, herunder kronisk obstruktiv lungesygdom (KOL), samt miljø og sundhed. Vi søger en motiveret og nysgerrig forsker, der ønsker at arbejde på tværs af fagområder, opbygge meningsfulde partnerskaber og bidrage til forskning, der tager udgangspunkt i lokalsamfundenes behov og prioriteter. Dine arbejdsopgaver Som postdoc får du mulighed for at udvikle din forskningsprofil og samtidig bidrage til praksisnær forskning med tydelig samfundsmæssig relevans. Dine primære arbejdsopgaver vil omfatte: Udvikling og evaluering af innovative indsatser: Bidrage til udvikling, implementering og evaluering af lokalsamfundsbaserede indsatser vedrørende kroniske lungesygdomme og relaterede udfordringer inden for miljø og sundhed med afsæt i lokalsamfundsinddragelse og implementeringsvidenskab. Videreudvikling af implementeringsvidenskab: Anvende og videreudvikle metodiske tilgange til at undersøge, hvordan evidensbaserede indsatser effektivt kan omsættes, tilpasses, implementeres og fastholdes i praksis. Inddragelse af lokalsamfund og interessenter: Samarbejde med borgere, patienter, sundhedsprofessionelle, forskere og andre relevante interessenter for at sikre, at forskningen afspejler deres erfaringer samt lokale prioriteter og praktiske behov. Gennemførelse af forskning af høj kvalitet: Bidrage til hypoteseudvikling, litteraturgennemgange, forskningsdesign, udvikling af spørgeskemaer, dataindsamling og -håndtering, kvalitetssikring af data samt kvalitative, kvantitative og mixed methods-analyser. Omsætning af forskningsresultater til praksis: Formidle forskningsresultater gennem fagfællebedømte publikationer, videnskabelige præsentationer, dialog med interessenter og lettilgængelige rapporter målrettet lokalsamfund. Udvikling af fremtidige forskningsmuligheder: Bidrage til fonds- og forskningsansøgninger, der understøtter udviklingen af innovativ implementeringsvidenskab med inddragelse af lokalsamfund. Udvikling af din forskerkarriere: Deltage i faglig udvikling, tværdisciplinært samarbejde og aktiviteter, der styrker din ekspertise inden for implementeringsvidenskab, forskning med lokalsamfundsinddragelse og vidensomsætning. Kvalifikationskrav Du skal have en ph.d.-grad eller tilsvarende inden for medicinsk videnskab, epidemiologi, folkesundhedsvidenskab, implementeringsvidenskab, samfundsvidenskab eller et beslægtet område. For at komme i betragtning til stillingen skal du have opnået din ph.d.-grad inden for de seneste fem år. Vi lægger vægt på, at du har: Gode mundtlige og skriftlige danskkundskaber samt stærke samarbejds- og kommunikationsevner. Stærke kvalitative og kvantitative forskningskompetencer, herunder erfaring med relevante implementeringsprojekter og analysemetoder. Erfaring med mixed methods-forskning samt statistisk og kvalitativ analysesoftware. Erfaring med digitale forskningsværktøjer og platforme såsom online spørgeskemaer, REDCap og NVivo. Erfaring med både videnskabelig og populærvidenskabelig formidling, eksempelvis via podcasts eller sociale medier. Stærke organisatoriske evner samt erfaring med projektledelse og problemløsning. Evne til at arbejde selvstændigt og samtidig bidrage aktivt til et tværfagligt forskningsmiljø. Et stærkt engagement i at forbedre sundhed og trivsel i lokalsamfund gennem grundig og inkluderende forskning med samfundsmæssig relevans. Vi ser gerne, at du har erfaring med eller særlig interesse for ét eller flere af følgende områder: Forskning med inddragelse af lokalsamfund, herunder lokalsamfundsbaseret eller deltagelsesbaseret forskning. Implementeringsvidenskab, formidling og implementering af forskning samt vidensomsætning. Mixed methods-forskning, der kombinerer kvalitative og kvantitative metoder. Teorier, modeller og rammeværk inden for implementeringsvidenskab. Forskning i kroniske lungesygdomme, miljø og sundhed, ulighed i sundhed eller beslægtede folkesundhedsudfordringer. Metoder og god praksis for meningsfuld inddragelse af lokalsamfund, samarbejde med interessenter og omsætning af forskning til praksis. Om Klinisk Institut Klinisk Institut varetager forskningsbaseret undervisning inden for alle discipliner på medicinuddannelsen og bedriver forskning inden for de kliniske specialer. Læs mere om Klinisk Institut her. Ansøgning Din ansøgning skal indeholde følgende: Ansøgning, hvori begrundelser for at ansøge, kvalifikationer i forhold til stillingen samt intentioner og visioner for stillingen angives CV Eksamensbeviser (kandidatbevis og ph.d.-bevis) Publikationsliste med angivelse af de vedhæftede publikationer, du ønsker tages i betragtning ved bedømmelsen. Du må maksimalt vedhæfte fem publikationer . Dokumentation for undervisningsmæssige kvalifikationer, hvis relevant. Formidlingsmæssige kvalifikationer, herunder deltagelse i udvalg, bestyrelser, foreninger o.l. Øvrige kvalifikationer i forhold til stillingen Referencer/anbefalinger Du kan læse mere om krav til din ansøgning her . Ansøgning sendes via Aalborg Universitets rekrutteringssystem, som kan tilgås under stillingsopslaget på Aalborg Universitets hjemmeside. Aalborg Universitet ønsker at afspejle det omgivende samfund og har diversitet som en kerneværdi. Derfor opfordres alle uanset personlig baggrund og orientering til at søge stillingen. Har du spørgsmål? Hvis du har spørgsmål stillingen, er du velkommen til at kontakte Professor og Ledende overlæge Ulla Møller Weinreich på tlf. +45 30687526. Samtaler forventes at blive afholdt den 25. november 2026. Øvrige informationer Du kan læse mere om vores rekrutteringsproces her . Ansættelsesprocessen på Aalborg Universitet indebærer en shortlistingsproces. Du kan læse mere om det her . Ansættelsesprocessen på Aalborg Universitet kan omfatte en risikovurdering som et værktøj til at identificere potentielle risici forbundet med nyansættelser, der sikrer arbejdspladsens sikkerhed, compliance og integritet. Løn- og ansættelsesvilkår Du ansættes i henhold til bekendtgørelse om ansættelse af videnskabeligt personale ved universiteter og bekendtgørelse om stillingsstruktur for videnskabeligt personale ved universiteter. Du ansættes og aflønnes desuden efter overenskomst for akademikere i staten og protokollat om visse ansættelsesvilkår for videnskabeligt personale ved universiteter. Du kan læse om lønnen og lønsammensætningen for stillingen i Lønoverblik i forbindelse med rekruttering - Videnskabelige stillinger (VIP) . Se det indledende afsnit på siden samt afsnittet ”Postdoc”. Der er 3 måneders gensidig prøvetid i stillingen. Aalborg Universitet - Viden for verden Aalborg Universitet er en international arbejdsplads med mere end 3700 ansatte. Vi udbyder virkelighedsnære uddannelser og skaber forskningsresultater i verdensklasse gennem samarbejde mellem forskere, studerende og offentlige og private virksomheder. Sådan opnås erkendelser, nye løsninger på samfundets problemer og viden, der forandrer verden. Vores hovedcampus ligger i Aalborg, men vi har også campus i Esbjerg og København. Employment type Fuldtid Ref number 2026/1227 Deadline 15.11.2026 Apply Employment and assessment Contact Contact Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 About AAU About AAU About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact Shortcuts Shortcuts EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions Service About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme"
    },
    "https://www.vacancies.aau.dk/scientific-positions/show-vacancy/vacancyId/983131": {
      "title": "One or more Postdoc positions in Optimization, AI and Autonomous Systems",
      "description": "One or more Postdoc positions in Optimization, AI and Autonomous Systems - Aalborg University Jump to content Vacant positions at Aalborg University Scientific positions Application requirements Recruitment process Career options PhD positions Application requirements PhD Schools Career options Recruitment process Technical or administrative positions Application requirements Appointment and assessment Career options AAU as a workplace Change language DA Search Vacant positions Scientific positions Show vacancy One or more Postdoc positions in Optimization, AI and Autonomous Systems Apply Vacant position One or more Postdoc positions in Optimization, AI and Autonomous Systems Aalborg Deadline : 15.11.2026 Department: Institut for Materialer og Produktion Ref number: 2026/1234 Employment type: Full Time Apply Aalborg Deadline : 15.11.2026 Department: Institut for Materialer og Produktion Ref number: 2026/1234 Employment type: Full Time Apply Vacant position One or more Postdoc positions in Optimization, AI and Autonomous Systems Aalborg Deadline : 15.11.2026 Department: Institut for Materialer og Produktion Ref number: 2026/1234 Employment type: Full Time Apply Aalborg Deadline : 15.11.2026 Department: Institut for Materialer og Produktion Ref number: 2026/1234 Employment type: Full Time Apply At the Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production one or more Postdoc positions in the area of Optimization and Algorithm Design are open for appointment from March 1st 2027 or soon thereafter. The position is for a period of three years Job description The positions are within the Operations Research (OR) group at Aalborg University and the research will be conducted in highly synergetic cooperation with leading Danish and European companies and international academic partners. The OR group focuses on solving complex problems, which require high-level modelling, data analysis and management capabilities as well as developing solution algorithms applying mathematical and computational approaches. The group has a particular focus on automated decision making in autonomous cyber-physical systems. The application area of the work covers a wide range of such systems spanning AGVs, UAVs, USVs, satellites, and more. These topics are also the ones addressed by this position. The applicant’s profile should therefore, ideally, address one or several of topics within AI: optimization algorithm (learning-based, heuristics, meta-heuristics, exact methods), MCDM (preference integration and mathematical modelling), algorithm design, development, and implementation. Your competencies We are looking for candidates with a strong interest in interdisciplinary research at the intersection of Computer Science, Operations Research, and Mathematics. Backgrounds in algorithm design and implementation, or machine learning or computational optimization and statistics along with strong programming skills, in e.g., Java, C, C++, R and Python, will be an advantage. The candidate is expected to contribute to ongoing research projects as well as participate in activities supporting future research projects and initiatives. As a successful applicant, you will participate in research projects with world-leading partners in areas such as: manufacturing, transportation, health care and aerospace. You will contribute to academic and collaborative research activities in the group and with external partners. You will also contribute to education activities in bachelor and master programs supported by the group. The candidate should be able to highlight research activities in the form of ISI’s Web of Science publications and the preferred candidate will also be able to demonstrate the application of research in practice. Appropriate candidates should have a master’s and PhD degree in Operations Research, Computer Science, Software Engineering, Applied Mathematics, Statistics, Robotics or a related field. Qualification requirements Appointment as postdoc requires academic qualifications at PhD level. How to apply Your application must include the following: Application, stating reasons for applying, qualifications in relation to the position, and intentions and visions for the position Curriculum Vitae (CV) Diplomas (master's degree diploma and PhD diploma) List of publications, with an indication of the attached publications that you wish to be taken into account in the assessment. You may attach a maximum of five publications. Documentation of teaching qualifications if relevant. Dissemination qualifications, including participation on committees or boards, participation in organisations etc. Additional qualifications in relation to the position References/recommendations You can read more about the requirements for your application here . The application must be submitted via Aalborg University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aalborg University's website. Aalborg University wants to reflect the surrounding society and has diversity as a core value. Therefore, everyone, regardless of personal background and orientation, is encouraged to apply for the position. Aalborg University has a policy of parallel language use. International staff are encouraged, with support from the university, to learn Danish during their employment in order to support their integration into the workplace and Danish society. Danish language courses will be offered as part of the employment. Do you have any questions? If you have any questions about the position, you are more than welcome to contact us. You will find contact persons at the bottom of the jobpost. Further information Read more about our recruitment process here The appointment process at Aalborg University involves a shortlisting process. You can read more about the shortlisting and appointment process here . The hiring process at Aalborg University may include a risk assessment as a tool to identify potential risks associated with new hires, ensuring the safety, compliance, and integrity of the workplace. Salary and terms of employment The employment is in accordance with the Ministerial Order on the Appointment of Academic Staff at Universities and the Ministerial Order on Job Structure for Academic Staff at Universities. Furthermore, your terms of employment and salary are in accordance with the collective agreement between the Danish Confederation of Professional Associations and the state (AC collective agreement) and protocol on certain terms of employment of academic staff at universities. You can find information about the salary and salary structure for the position in the Salary Overview for Recruitment - Scientific positions (VIP) . Please refer to the introductory section of the page and the section entitled “Postdoc”. There is a mutual probationary period of 3 months for the position. Aalborg University - Knowledge for the world Aalborg University is an international workplace with more than 3,700 employees. We offer real-world-oriented education and create world-class research results through collaboration between researchers, students, and public and private companies. This is how we achieve insights, new solutions to societal problems, and knowledge that changes the world. Our main campus is in Aalborg, but we also have campuses in Esbjerg and Copenhagen. Contacts Peter Nielsen: +4599408932, peter@mp.aau.dk HR Support : +4599403031 Employment type Full time Ref number 2026/1234 Deadline 15.11.2026 Apply Employment and assessment Contact Contact Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 About AAU About AAU About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact Shortcuts Shortcuts EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions Service About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme"
    },
    "https://www.vacancies.aau.dk/scientific-positions/show-vacancy/vacancyId/983337": {
      "title": "Postdoc in Resilient Satellite and Quantum Networks",
      "description": "Postdoc in Resilient Satellite and Quantum Networks - Aalborg University Jump to content Vacant positions at Aalborg University Scientific positions Application requirements Recruitment process Career options PhD positions Application requirements PhD Schools Career options Recruitment process Technical or administrative positions Application requirements Appointment and assessment Career options AAU as a workplace Change language DA Search Vacant positions Scientific positions Show vacancy Postdoc in Resilient Satellite and Quantum Networks Apply Vacant position Postdoc in Resilient Satellite and Quantum Networks Aalborg Deadline : 16.11.2026 Department: Department of Electronic Systems Ref number: 2026/1249 Employment type: Full Time Apply Aalborg Deadline : 16.11.2026 Department: Department of Electronic Systems Ref number: 2026/1249 Employment type: Full Time Apply Vacant position Postdoc in Resilient Satellite and Quantum Networks Aalborg Deadline : 16.11.2026 Department: Department of Electronic Systems Ref number: 2026/1249 Employment type: Full Time Apply Aalborg Deadline : 16.11.2026 Department: Department of Electronic Systems Ref number: 2026/1249 Employment type: Full Time Apply At the Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, a position as postdoc in Resilient Satellite Networks with Classical and Quantum Communications is open for appointment from 1 February 2027, or as soon as possible thereafter. The position is available for 24 months. In electronic engineering, Aalborg University is known worldwide for its high academic quality and societal impact. The Department of Electronic Systems employs more than 200 people, of which about 90 are PhD students, and about 40 % of all employees are internationals. In total, it has more than 600 students in its BSc and MSc programs, which are based on AAU's problem-based learning model. The department leverages its unique research infrastructure and lab facilities to conduct world-leading fundamental and applied research within communication, networks, control systems, AI, sound, cyber security, and robotics. The department plays an active role in transferring inventions and results into applications in close collaboration with industrial partners worldwide. You can read more about the department at www.es.aau.dk. Your work tasks In this postdoctoral position you will play a central role towards developing techniques to model integrated satellite and terrestrial communication networks as dynamic graphs based on the spatial characteristics, orbital dynamics, and timing requirements of the system. You will work in an international and interdisciplinary environment with experts in mobile communication networks, satellite communications, quantum communications, statistics, and artificial intelligence. Your main responsibility will be to develop techniques to model integrated mobile and satellite communication networks as dynamic graphs based on the spatial characteristics and orbital dynamics of the system, both for classical and quantum communications. You’ll investigate feature extraction and graph representation learning algorithms, as well as algorithms method for formulating and solving link establishment, matching, and routing problems on the network graphs using both classical graph theory and AI methods such as graph neural networks (GNNs). You will also develop distribution-free methods for reliability guarantees, using conformal prediction to provide calibrated, finite-sample guarantees on link performance and on the fidelity of entanglement distributed over satellite and terrestrial links. A key aspect of your work will be to model the spatial and temporal aspects of classical and quantum communication systems, as well as system disruptions, to enable the statistical evaluation and improvement of the resilience of the network to failures. Furthermore, you’ll work on decentralized algorithms to adapt the operation of the network to achieve the target network resilience with minimal performance loss. Your competences You have completed a PhD in electrical engineering, telecommunications, statistics, information theory, applied mathematics, data science, or a closely related field. You are comfortable working with abstract concepts in information and graph theory and statistics, and you enjoy translating them into concrete algorithms. You have experience with information- and communication-theoretic modelling, programming, probability, statistics, and AI. You bring documented experience with publishing research in recognised international journals and conferences, and you are motivated by contributing to the international research community through high-quality publications. Ideally, you are familiar with at least one of the following domains: wireless communications, graph theory, applied mathematics, statistics and AI. Knowledge on satellite networks and quantum communications is beneficial but not required. We are looking for motivated, proactive and curious candidates, who enjoy working at the intersection of several disciplines and are comfortable taking initiative in developing new research ideas. You thrive in a collaborative research environment where ideas are openly discussed, where feedback is part of the daily work, and where results are developed in close dialogue with colleagues from different backgrounds. At the same time, you can work independently, plan your work, and drive your own projects forward. You communicate clearly in writing and in speech, and you can present complex concepts in an accessible way to colleagues from other disciplines. Proficiency in English at C1 level or above is required for this position, both for scientific writing and for daily collaboration in an international environment. Who we are The postdoc will be hired at the Connectivity Section of the Department of Electronic Systems of Aalborg University under project “STATSAT: STATistical methods for provable resilient and scalable SATellite networks,” funded by Villum Fonden and “CLASSIQUE: Center for Classical Communication in the Quantum Era,” funded by the Danish National Research Foundation (DNRF). You will work as part of the Satellites and Space Communications research group and CLASSIQUE Center of Excellence, and will collaborate with researchers from the Classical and Quantum Information and Connectivity research group, and of the Department of Mathematical Sciences. The Connectivity section works on concepts for communication and networking in wireless systems, such as the emerging 6G technology, but also in a broader sense, using methods of communication theory. It hosts two research groups: Classical and Quantum Information and Connectivity (CQUIC) and Satellites and Space Communications (SSC). CQUIC works on communication and information processing in classical and quantum communication networks. It places particular emphasis on wireless connectivity and on the interplay among AI, computation, and communication. Its core approach combines communication-theoretic analysis with experimental studies of wireless systems. SSC conducts research in satellite and space systems for communications, sensing, computing, and AI. Combines methodologies from communication theory, graph-based analysis, and stochastic systems with data-driven modeling, analysis, and optimization for diverse space systems and applications. Qualification requirements Appointment as postdoc requires academic qualifications at PhD level. How to apply Your application must include the following: Application, stating reasons for applying, qualifications in relation to the position, and intentions and visions for the position Curriculum Vitae (CV) Diplomas (master's degree diploma and PhD diploma) List of publications, with an indication of the attached publications that you wish to be taken into account in the assessment. You may attach a maximum of five publications. Documentation of teaching qualifications if relevant. Dissemination qualifications, including participation on committees or boards, participation in organisations etc. Additional qualifications in relation to the position References/recommendations You can read more about the requirements for your application here . The application must be submitted via Aalborg University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aalborg University's website. Aalborg University wants to reflect the surrounding society and has diversity as a core value. Therefore, everyone, regardless of personal background and orientation, is encouraged to apply for the position. Aalborg University has a policy of parallel language use. International staff are encouraged, with support from the university, to learn Danish during their employment in order to support their integration into the workplace and Danish society. Danish language courses will be offered as part of the employment. Do you have any questions? If you have any questions about the position, you are more than welcome to contact us. You will find contact persons at the bottom of the jobpost. Further information Read more about our recruitment process here The appointment process at Aalborg University involves a shortlisting process. You can read more about the shortlisting and appointment process here . The hiring process at Aalborg University may include a risk assessment as a tool to identify potential risks associated with new hires, ensuring the safety, compliance, and integrity of the workplace. Salary and terms of employment The employment is in accordance with the Ministerial Order on the Appointment of Academic Staff at Universities and the Ministerial Order on Job Structure for Academic Staff at Universities. Furthermore, your terms of employment and salary are in accordance with the collective agreement between the Danish Confederation of Professional Associations and the state (AC collective agreement) and protocol on certain terms of employment of academic staff at universities. You can find information about the salary and salary structure for the position in the Salary Overview for Recruitment - Scientific positions (VIP) . Please refer to the introductory section of the page and the section entitled “Postdoc”. Aalborg University - Knowledge for the world Aalborg University is an international workplace with more than 3,700 employees. We offer real-world-oriented education and create world-class research results through collaboration between researchers, students, and public and private companies. This is how we achieve insights, new solutions to societal problems, and knowledge that changes the world. Our main campus is in Aalborg, but we also have campuses in Esbjerg and Copenhagen. Contacts Petar Popovski: petarp@es.aau.dk HR Support : Aau-hrsupport@adm.aau.dk Employment type Full time Ref number 2026/1249 Deadline 16.11.2026 Apply Employment and assessment Contact Contact Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 About AAU About AAU About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact Shortcuts Shortcuts EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions Service About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme"
    },
